  "record_format": "FS_READBACK_TRACE schema=1 seq=<u64> us=<u64> event=<name> a=<u64> b=<u64> c=<u64>",
  "status_format": "FS_READBACK_TRACE_STATUS schema=1 reserved=<usize> drained=<usize> dropped=<usize> io_errors=<usize> capacity=2048",
  "ordering": "seq is atomic reservation order; us is monotonic-clock elapsed from first screenshot preparation. Concurrent recording can reorder timestamps relative to reservations. No total causality is implied. Drain publishes only contiguous fully written slots. Status is a non-atomic concurrent snapshot, not a process-final completeness attestation.",
  "limits": [
    "The sole screenshot entity and the existing screenshot-transfer-buffer label bind this one-capture recipe. This is not a general multi-screenshot recorder.",
    "A callback may run before core_map_return; receive_resumed may precede channel_send_return. Only established program/channel ordering is causal.",
    "callback_invoke wraps exactly the selected original callback, including synchronous errors; callback_return is absent on original panic. No original None callback is replaced.",
    "maintain_return mapping count includes all mappings on the selected device. Use selected handle_map_return plus callback_invoke as per-buffer evidence.",
    "main_receive and event_queued show receipt and queued Bevy command, not observer execution or PNG save. Ordinary log/PNG/process checks establish those.",
    "Writes are best effort, statuses are concurrent snapshots, and a stalled main loop may leave an undrained tail. Drop/gap/I/O errors or missing final drain preclude proof of absence. First overflow is reported once; later dropped counts need not be emitted.",
    "No pointer addresses, pixels, buffer bytes, or shader/model bytes are exported. BufferId index and epoch are engine object identifiers."
  ]
